[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501111014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119603#issuecomment-4501111014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119603","id":4501111014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDEmA5g","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T17:55:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T17:55:39Z","body":"Hi @ElectricGrizzly , since you mentioned you remember being able to do this in earlier versions of Godot 4.x, would you be able to test some previous stable versions (e.g. the 4.5 and 4.4 branches) so we can identify if this is a recent regression or a longer standing issue? This sounds like a bug to me so it would be good to confirm, but I'm not as familiar with the C#/dotnet side of the engine.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501111014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540172830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119603#issuecomment-4540172830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119603","id":4540172830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDp2KHg","user":{"login":"norepro","id":30921834,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTIxODM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30921834?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro","html_url":"https://github.com/norepro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T04:52:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T04:52:17Z","body":"Sounds like a bug to me too. I opened a PR that I think addresses it. Similar logic already exists elsewhere in the engine, but you found a case that was missing that treatment. Basically the editor was passing the non-tool resource as a native placeholder script instead of a proper C# script, causing the type mismatch.\n\nI do not know when the flaw was introduced, but I saw the exception as far back as 4.2 stable. I did not try any builds before that. It's an old one!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540172830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4542304658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119603#issuecomment-4542304658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119603","id":4542304658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDr4Rkg","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T08:45:07Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T08:45:07Z","body":"Only tool scripts are constructed and run in the editor, so I don't think this would have ever worked, and it doesn't seem like a bug to me. If you need the resource instance to be available when running in the editor, annotate the type with `[Tool]` so it's also a tool script. Otherwise, export it as `Resource` instead of using the concrete type.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4542304658/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4543874631","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119603#issuecomment-4543874631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119603","id":4543874631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDtYGRw","user":{"login":"norepro","id":30921834,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTIxODM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30921834?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro","html_url":"https://github.com/norepro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T11:44:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T11:57:28Z","body":"> Only tool scripts are constructed and run in the editor, so I don't think this would have ever worked, and it doesn't seem like a bug to me. If you need the resource instance to be available when running in the editor, annotate the type with `[Tool]` so it's also a tool script. Otherwise, export it as `Resource` instead of using the concrete type.\n\nMakes sense. I can adjust the change to instead show a more friendly error, something like this?\n\n>   ERROR: modules/mono/glue/runtime_interop.cpp:246 - Cannot access non-[Tool] C# script from the editor. Consider adding the [Tool] attribute to: res://CustomResource.cs\n\nEDIT: Updated PR to show that error.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4543874631/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4972627144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119603#issuecomment-4972627144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119603","id":4972627144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKGREyA","user":{"login":"WalkerWhite","id":3065109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjUxMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3065109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite","html_url":"https://github.com/WalkerWhite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalkerWhite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T18:30:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T18:30:09Z","body":"### Tested Versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.3.stable.mono.official [7d41c59c4]\n\n### System Information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable.mono - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 Max (Apple8) - Apple M2 Max (12 threads) - 64.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue Description\n\nI have been able to reproduce the error above but it is actually a _different_ problem than what is discussed in this thread. Initial attempts to annotate the custom resource class with `[Tool]` did not cause the error to go away.  Instead, the problem seems to be with how C# annotations are parsed.  \n\nThis annotation causes Godot to crash with the error above when the resource is used in the editor:\n\n```\n[Tool, GlobalClass]\npublic partial class CustomResource : Resource\n{\n}\n```\n\nOn the other hand, this annotation works correctly:\n\n```\n[Tool]\n[GlobalClass]\npublic partial class CustomResource : Resource\n{\n}\n```\n\nMy understanding is that these are supposed to be equivalent, but Godot is not treating them as such.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4972627144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]